text:
Q: How do I use CSS selectors to select the child of a parent&#39;s sibling when a child is hovered? A: <p>You are almost there. It's a mix of both on the #main div.</p>
<p>Like :</p>
<pre><code>&lt;style&gt;
.style1, .style2 {
    display:none;
}
#main:has(.hover1:hover) .style1 {
    display: block;
}

#main:has(.hover2:hover) .style2 {
    display: block;
}
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;main&quot;&gt;
  text that the text below goes under&lt;br&gt;

  &lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;hover1&quot;&gt;reveals style1 text when hovered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;hover2&quot;&gt;reveals style2 text when hovered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;style1&quot;&gt;words words words&lt;br&gt;
    words words words&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;style2&quot;&gt;different words&lt;br&gt;
    words words words&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;hover1&quot;&gt;reveals style1 text when hovered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;hover2&quot;&gt;reveals style2 text when hovered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;style1&quot;&gt;words words words&lt;br&gt;
    words words words&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class=&quot;style2&quot;&gt;different words&lt;br&gt;
    words words words&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
